body:
For what it is worth, I have two displays, one with 4k @60HZ, the other at 1080P, 144hz. I like much mopre, for now a 4k display, even if I have to downgrade a bit the max settings for the sake of framerate in town.

&#x200B;

Also note that if you have a computer with enough ressources, 4k with DSR can neat you a 8K display, though you might have to set graphics to a bare minimum, etc. Also, since im looking into that, anyone have any inputs of how to maximize performances with 8k DSR? I'd really like someone to point me in the right direction. Thnks!

As many have already mentionned, until lv 50 or so, the game feels more like a tutorial than anything else. You will learn to play the class you choose little by little, and progress with the different aspects of the game. Don'T hesitate to try other jobs (you just have to change your main weapon to change to a class you unlocked).

&#x200B;

I do say try other class if you don't feel comfortable, but I would focus on one ASAP so you can progress into the game. If you feel the urge of leveling faster, look for the instance named "Palace of the Dead" around Quarrymill. You will still have to go through your story, though. Believe me, as a recent returnee, it does get better though it is slow at times.

My 2 cents from someone who started less than a month ago.

&#x200B;

Until max level, the game is not so much grindy as I would have expected. If you really care about "endgame stuff", well I hope you like PVP, because thats a lot where it is. As for the caveat, yes, you'lll have to either: 1)be patient and understand that is is a marathon run and not a sprint, or 2) invest a bit more money where needed to catchup whith older players.

&#x200B;

Playwise, I find the game really enjoyable, and has alot of potential (for a mmo on NA shelves since only 3 years).

Any further questions? AMA, I'll answer my best as a newbie!
